diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index 410d02489a..f60cd1ec42 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ Version 1.8.0 (2026-10-06)
 
 Enhancements
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
+- The metadata returned by :meth:`moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm.get_data` has two new columns: ``dataset``, the code of the dataset each trial comes from (for a :class:`~moabb.datasets.compound_dataset.CompoundDataset`, the dataset the subject comes from), and ``device``, the recording device. ``device`` is the canonical name of ``METADATA.acquisition.hardware`` given by :func:`moabb.datasets.metadata.devices.canonical_device` (the 107 free-text descriptions map to 30 devices, e.g. every spelling of the g.tec g.USBamp; ``"unknown"`` when the dataset gives none); :class:`moabb.datasets.Peters2026` returns the DSI-24 or DSI-Flex of each visit. ``CrossSubjectEvaluation(cv_class=LeaveOneGroupOut, groups="dataset")`` holds out one dataset at a time and ``groups="device"`` one device at a time, and :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossDatasetSplitter` works on paradigm output (:gh:`1328` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :meth:`moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm.get_data` no longer fails when the recordings it stacks have different channels or numbers of samples, e.g. datasets with different montages or sampling rates pooled in a :class:`~moabb.datasets.compound_dataset.CompoundDataset`: it returns a nested object array of shape ``(n_trials,)`` holding each trial's ``(n_channels, n_times)`` array, and the evaluations accept it, so leave-one-dataset-out runs with :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossSubjectEvaluation` and ``cv_class=LeaveOneGroupOut``. Recordings of one shape still give a regular array; ``return_epochs=True`` raises a clear error for such recordings, as ``mne.Epochs`` cannot hold them (:gh:`1327` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Versioned documentation: release tags (``v*``) deploy the "stable" docs to https://moabb.neurotechx.com/docs/ and ``develop`` deploys the "dev" docs to https://moabb.neurotechx.com/dev/, so the default documentation matches the PyPI release; a version switcher in the navbar (``_static/versions.json``) moves between them (:gh:`445`, :gh:`983` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.PerezBlanco2026`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Wang2026` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Han2026` read from NEMAR: PerezBlanco2026 and Wang2026 take the subject's original files from the published deposits ``nm000304`` and ``nm000335`` (``nemar_seed_cache``; Wang2026 declares the deposit's ``sub-<id>`` subject labels), and Han2026 reads NEMAR's raw import of OpenNeuro ds007327 (``on007327``) before OpenNeuro. The private deposits of Brodu2012 (``nm000366``), Lenaig2026 (``nm000333``), MartinezPeon2025 (``nm000332``), MIBMPI2024 (``nm000331``) and MIND2026 (``nm000337``) get their ``nemar_id`` once published (:gh:`1318` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
